<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27385" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lyncestae</span></b> , ārum,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λυγκησταί</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a people in the
				south-western part of Macedonia</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 45,
				30, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 10, 17, §
			35</span></i>.— Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lyncestĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., Lyncestian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amnis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 15, 329</span></i>
			; v. <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 3, 20 <i>fin.</i></span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lyncestis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f.
			<i>adj., Lyncestian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aqua,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					2, 103, 106, § 230</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lyncestus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>adj., Lyncestian</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 8, 3,
				17</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
